# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: dxf-angles-probe-accoreconsole-export -- on accoreconsole the dxf-angles probe stops at the DXF export (COM SaveAs), before its SAVEAS fallback
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom

dxf-angles:probe:accoreconsole:windows (jobs 17409369692, 17411108963):
all 18 cases are created and reported, then the run ends right before
the export -- DXFANG-INCOMPLETE, no EXPORT line, no DXF. AutoCAD GUI
(17411108962) and both BricsCADs export through COM vla-SaveAs and are
complete.

accoreconsole has no COM: (vl-load-com) / (vlax-get-acad-object) /
vla-SaveAs there apparently abort the run although the call is inside
vl-catch-all-apply (cf. the cad-probe pitfalls: some failures escape the
catch on AutoCAD).

* Fix

Skip the COM export when (getvar "PROGRAM") is "accoreconsole" (or when
vlax-get-acad-object is not callable) and go straight to the
(command "_.SAVEAS" "_DXF" "16" path) form; then check that SAVEAS
prompt sequence on accoreconsole. Not needed for the angle verification
(AutoCAD GUI is the same DXF writer and was measured), only to have the
accoreconsole lane complete.

* Fixed and verified (2026-10-23, MR !474, 2.3.44) -- DONE

The probe skips COM when the run script says it is accoreconsole
(DXFANG_BACKEND): dxf-angles:probe:accoreconsole:windows (job
17414697754) printed "EXPORT vla-SaveAs skipped (accoreconsole: no COM)",
then "EXPORT command-SAVEAS-DXF ok", read the file back and reached
DXFANG-DONE; its DXF is in the artefact.
